# Welcome!

#### This professional learning module prepares you to teach **Foundations of AI Programming**—a unit that introduces students to programming fundamentals using Python (sequence, selection, iteration, functions), algorithms, and ethical computing, emphasizing human-centered design for inclusive, real-world problem-solving.
.

___

<div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; width: 95%; margin: 20pt auto; padding: 0 5px;">
  <img src="https://images.code.org/36211eedb3698751fa5523b4dde93351-image-1760467094025.png" style="border-radius: 5pt; width: 32%;">
  <img src="https://images.code.org/7f813b0aec7d472e470f94eb91471aa1-image-1760466945803.png" style="border-radius: 5pt; width: 32%;">
  <img src="https://images.code.org/ddb463a06ccc88f5d7390a1f841a0f31-image-1760467013014.png" style="border-radius: 5pt; width: 32%;">
</div>

___


#### **By the end of this professional learning module, you will be able to:**

* #### Prepare to teach foundational AI programming concepts by modeling computational thinking and core programming constructs, including variables, functions, loops, and conditionals.

* #### Guide students in reasoning about program behavior and decision making, including nested conditionals and ethical considerations in algorithmic systems.

* #### Prepare students for a culminating project by guiding them through a structured, multi-day design and development process that includes brainstorming and decomposition, iterative coding with peer feedback, and reflection on both their creative choices and responsible AI use.

## Take Our Pre-Survey

#### To better gauge your learning and improve this professional learning module, please take our pre-survey - it will take fewer than five minutes to complete.

<div style="margin: 20px 0px">
<a class="btn btn-large btn-primary" href="https://studio.code.org/form/selfpaced_pd_teaching_aif_programming_pre_survey" target="blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Take the Pre-Survey</a>
</div>

### **Suggested total time for this module:** 120 minutes
#### *Teaching Foundations of AI Programming is broken up into two 60 minute lessons. When you're done with Part 1, continue onto Part 2.*



 


